# TASK-260715-3cv3r4 rework outcome

## Result

Ready for review. All four findings from `TASK-260715-3cv3r4_review-results.md` are closed with fake-only behavioral tests. No real Keychain, SSH/network, NetworkExtension, VPN, route, DNS, interface, or packet-filter operation ran.

## Rework closure

- Every `SSHHostKeyDecision` case (`acceptMatch`, `acceptApproved`, `trustRequired`, changed, revoked, algorithm, host-mismatch, malformed, and policy rejection) traverses the candidate-neutral `SSHTransport` fixture. Every rejecting path records only `hostPolicy`, with zero credential lookup, signature/authentication, direct-channel, exec-channel, or open-request work.
- The bounded resource snapshot now accounts for task, connection, channel, socket, descriptor, buffered bytes, observer, and callback counts. During a gated cancellation it observes one active task/connection/observer/callback, then returns to the same zero baseline after cancellation. Sixteen bounded iterations also restore baseline after success and rejection.
- `LiveMacOSSystemKeychainSecurityClient` has an internal injectable matcher. A synthetic fixture query returns `errSecParam` before the matcher; the spy records zero calls. The fixture constructor and matcher remain non-public, and exact one-item reference/search-list behavior has no fallback or enumeration.
- Invalid generation, noncanonical host, unsupported schema, and prohibited-secret profile classes traverse the real `TunnelRuntimeCoordinator` startup boundary. Injected Keychain and network fake counters remain zero for every invalid case; the valid control reaches each exactly once.

